{
  "action": "check_meters",
  "note": "The tin is in my tray, seal intact. That's enough. I don't owe Phil a story about a name my brother whispered into a mic in a kitchen that no longer exists. I check the line meter, confirm the channel is clean, and let the lamp burn its last eighty seconds. The handoff is mine to shape. I will give this broadcast a voice that is not the wire's voice. Mercury stays in the drawer. The combination is 5066 and it stays 5066. I slide my thumb across the fader, listen to the room tone, and wait for my cue. Phil can have his weather card when the clock says so. Right now the meters are mine and the air is mine and that is the whole arrangement."
}
